{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39835968",
      "title": "Splitting CSS Code Across Multiple Files",
      "sourceHash": "ff6b46ed18e405b9b150f5abc064789cbcc48d049f5196fb23934107296af4cf",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 3.96,
          "en": "So as mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.96,
          "end": 8.94,
          "en": "when it comes to styling React apps, you got many options.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.94,
          "end": 13.92,
          "en": "And one option definitely is to simply add a CSS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 13.92,
          "end": 17.28,
          "en": "to your project like this index CSS file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 17.28,
          "end": 22.28,
          "en": "Define all your CSS rules in there, using element selectors,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 23.76,
          "end": 27.63,
          "en": "using ID selectors, using class selectors.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 27.63,
          "end": 32.172,
          "en": "So any CSS rules you can define, define them in here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 32.172,
          "end": 36.099,
          "en": "then import this CSS file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 36.099,
          "end": 40.02,
          "en": "And as you learned earlier in this course already,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 40.02,
          "end": 42.3,
          "en": "in a typical React project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 42.3,
          "end": 45.72,
          "en": "for example, in this project here, which uses Vite",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 45.72,
          "end": 48.12,
          "en": "as an underlying development and build tool,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 48.12,
          "end": 53.12,
          "en": "you can import CSS files into JavaScript files like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 53.52,
          "end": 57.72,
          "en": "And the build tool, so Vite in this case here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 57.72,
          "end": 61.74,
          "en": "will identify such imports and in the end simply make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 61.74,
          "end": 64.602,
          "en": "that the CSS file you are trying to import here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 64.602,
          "end": 69.03,
          "en": "gets injected into this webpage, which is served here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 69.03,
          "end": 72.72,
          "en": "Therefore, if you open the developer tools on your website",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 72.72,
          "end": 74.875,
          "en": "you will see that in the head section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 74.875,
          "end": 79.875,
          "en": "this style here was dynamically injected by Vite.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 80.905,
          "end": 84.69,
          "en": "So in here you find all the styles that are defined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 84.69,
          "end": 88.28,
          "en": "in index CSS, and this was added dynamically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 88.28,
          "end": 91.33,
          "en": "to the DOM here by Vite.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 91.33,
          "end": 94.28999999999999,
          "en": "So that's how that works",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 94.28999999999999,
          "end": 98.34,
          "en": "and therefore you can include vanilla CSS files like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 98.34,
          "end": 102.09,
          "en": "and you can of course include as many vanilla CSS files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 102.09,
          "end": 103.213,
          "en": "as you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 103.213,
          "end": 107.64,
          "en": "You don't have to go with a single CSS file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 107.64,
          "end": 110.16,
          "en": "Instead you can add as many as you want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 110.16,
          "end": 114.47999999999999,
          "en": "and you could, for example, therefore also split this file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 114.47999999999999,
          "end": 117.6,
          "en": "into multiple files where you attach",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 117.6,
          "end": 121.443,
          "en": "the individual files to the Components to which they belong.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 122.58,
          "end": 124.68,
          "en": "For example, here we could say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 124.68,
          "end": 127.56,
          "en": "that the header specific styles,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 127.56,
          "end": 130.17,
          "en": "so all these rules here in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 130.17,
          "end": 133.44,
          "en": "should go into a separate header CSS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 133.44,
          "end": 137.403,
          "en": "which maybe is co-located next to this header JSX file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 138.27100000000002,
          "end": 142.572,
          "en": "So we could add a header CSS file here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 142.572,
          "end": 147.03,
          "en": "and then just grab these header related styles,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 147.03,
          "end": 152.03,
          "en": "cut them from index CSS, and add them here in header CSS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 153.542,
          "end": 156.96,
          "en": "And then with that in header JSX,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 156.96,
          "end": 159.72,
          "en": "we can of course also add such a import,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 159.72,
          "end": 161.587,
          "en": "which imports from header.CSS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 164.08100000000002,
          "end": 165.72,
          "en": "And with those changes applied,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 165.72,
          "end": 167.88,
          "en": "if you save that and you reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 167.88,
          "end": 170.88,
          "en": "you'll see that the page still looks the same",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 170.88,
          "end": 174.99,
          "en": "as it did before because of course now this import here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 174.99,
          "end": 178.68,
          "en": "is also resolved by Vite js, and the styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 178.68,
          "end": 182.73,
          "en": "defined in the header CSS file are therefore also injected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 182.73,
          "end": 184.62,
          "en": "into this webpage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 184.62,
          "end": 187.59,
          "en": "As you can still see if you open the developer tools,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 187.59,
          "end": 189.09,
          "en": "there in the head section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 189.09,
          "end": 192.81,
          "en": "we now got two injected style tags here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 192.81,
          "end": 195.506,
          "en": "one which includes the header styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 195.506,
          "end": 197.117,
          "en": "and then the other one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 197.117,
          "end": 200.913,
          "en": "which includes all the other styles from the index CSS file.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}